From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:08:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wineboot: Do not start a second services.exe.

In a new prefix wineboot --init runs twice when it is the command run: once for the first process,
which starts the prefix, and then as that process.  Each started a services.exe, and the two then
served the same pipe and started the same services.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
index 167b685f580..76d066c5f07 100644
--- a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
+++ b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
@@ -1502,6 +1502,16 @@ static BOOL start_services_process(void)
     HANDLE wait_handles[2], token;
     BOOL ret;
 
+    /* not a second one, as when this runs twice in a new prefix: once for the first process, and then as
+     * that process, "wineboot --init" */
+    if ((wait_handles[0] = OpenEventW( SYNCHRONIZE, FALSE, svcctl_started_event )))
+    {
+        WINE_TRACE( "services.exe is running already\n" );
+        WaitForSingleObject( wait_handles[0], INFINITE );
+        CloseHandle( wait_handles[0] );
+        return TRUE;
+    }
+
     /* in this session if it cannot be moved, as before */
     token = get_services_token();
     ret = create_native_process( token, L"C:\\windows\\system32\\services.exe", NULL,
